## Summary

Made changes in two files, both under the disposable run root.

**`src/types.ts`** — Added `"storehouse"` to the `BuildingKind` union:
```ts
export type BuildingKind = "hut" | "farm" | "quarry" | "storehouse";
```

**`src/sim.ts`**
1. Added the storehouse cost to `BUILDING_COSTS`:
   ```ts
   storehouse: { wood: 25, stone: 10 },
   ```
2. Added a new `BUILDING_PREREQUISITES` record mapping each building kind to the buildings required before it becomes available (empty for all except storehouse):
   ```ts
   export const BUILDING_PREREQUISITES: Record<BuildingKind, BuildingKind[]> = {
     hut: [], farm: [], quarry: [],
     storehouse: ["hut"],
   };
   ```
3. Added the requested export:
   ```ts
   export function availableBuildings(settlement: Settlement): BuildingKind[] {
     return (Object.keys(BUILDING_COSTS) as BuildingKind[]).filter((kind) => {
       if (!canAfford(settlement, kind)) return false;
       return BUILDING_PREREQUISITES[kind].every((required) =>
         settlement.buildings.includes(required),
       );
     });
   }
   ```

The function iterates every building kind, keeps those that `canAfford` accepts, and additionally requires all of the kind's prerequisite buildings to already be present in `settlement.buildings`. Kinds with no prerequisites (empty array) pass the `every` check vacuously, so "hut"/"farm"/"quarry" are governed solely by affordability, matching the requirement.

Verified: `npm run typecheck` (tsc --noEmit) passes, and `npm run test` (vitest) passes — 4/4 existing tests green. No source fixtures or sibling checkouts were touched.


